# Repository attributes — mostly about keeping merges clean for a team on mixed
# operating systems. See CONTRIBUTING.md for the workflow these support.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- line endings

# The single most valuable line here.
#
# Without it, each clone's line endings depend on that machine's local
# core.autocrlf. A teammate whose setting differs commits a file with CRLF, and
# git sees EVERY LINE as changed — a 900-line file conflicts with itself, and
# the real one-line change is invisible in the diff.
#
# `text=auto` makes git normalise to LF in the repository regardless of local
# config, while still checking out each platform's native endings. Every tracked
# text file in this repo is already stored as LF, so adding this changes nothing
# on disk — it just stops the situation from ever arising.
* text=auto

# ------------------------------------------------------------- binary content

# Git cannot merge these. Marking them explicitly means it does not try, does
# not print megabytes of garbage into a diff, and fails loudly (both versions
# kept, pick one) rather than producing a corrupt file.
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# NetCDF sample data — binary, and the committed fixtures are regenerable with
# `backend/snapshot_fixtures.py`.
*.nc    binary

# SVG is XML, so leave it mergeable, but the MoES marks are largely base64 blobs
# and a diff of them is noise.
*.svg   -diff

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ generated

# Lockfiles are generated, not authored. Collapsed in review because a diff of
# them tells a reviewer nothing.
#
# NEVER hand-resolve a conflict in these. Take main's copy and regenerate:
#     git checkout --theirs package-lock.json && npm install
# Hand-editing a lockfile produces a tree that installs differently for
# different people, which is a genuinely nasty class of bug to chase.
package-lock.json          -diff linguist-generated=true
frontend/package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true

# ------------------------------------------------------------ GitHub language

# Reference material for the editor tooling, not project source. Without this,
# ~5,000 lines of bundled Three.js notes dominate GitHub's language bar and the
# repo reads as a Markdown project.
.claude/skills/** linguist-documentation

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- notes
#
# Deliberately NOT set: a `merge=union` driver on context.md.
#
# The decision log in §10 is append-only and would genuinely benefit from union
# merging, but .gitattributes applies a merge driver to a whole FILE, and
# context.md is 700 lines of structured prose and tables. Union-merging all of
# it would silently keep BOTH sides of any edited paragraph — producing a file
# that merges cleanly and reads as nonsense, which is worse than a conflict you
# can see. The convention in CONTRIBUTING.md handles it instead.
